  "prefLabel": "Bar 101.54 Threading",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Bar 101.54 \"Threading\" means a service provided by a master barber, cosmetologist, or esthetician that results in the removal of hair from its follicle from around the eyebrows and from other parts of the face with the use of a single strand of thread and an astringent. The meaning does not include the use of chemicals of any kind, wax, or any implements, instruments, or tools to remove hair.\n\nSource. #14459, eff 1-1-26",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/bar100-700.html"
